<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>YOBC France Tour 2026 — Tour Route</name><description>Numbered stops in tour order, July 27 - August 6, 2026</description><Style id="route"><LineStyle><color>ffE07A38</color><width>4</width></LineStyle></Style><Folder><name>Stops in order</name><Placemark><name>1. JFK International Airport</name><description>Departure Day — Monday, July 27

John F. Kennedy International Airport in Queens, New York. American Airlines terminal for transatlantic flights.

Schedule:
Monday, July 27 TBD: Meet at BCCC — transfer by bus to JFK
Monday, July 27 6:59 PM: Flight AA0198 departs JFK
Thursday, August 6 2:10 PM: Arrive JFK — bus back to BCCC

Address: Queens, NY 11430</description><Point><coordinates>-73.7781,40.6413,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Milan Malpensa Airport</name><description>Day 1 — Tuesday, July 28

Milan&#x27;s main international airport, gateway to Northern Italy and the Alps. Flight AA0198 arrives here from JFK.

Schedule:
Tuesday, July 28 11:10 AM: Arrive Milan Malpensa — meet coaches and guides
Thursday, August 6 11:10 AM: Flight AA0199 departs Milan — arrives JFK 2:10 PM

Address: Via dell&#x27;Aeroporto, 21013 Casorate Sempione VA, Italy</description><Point><coordinates>8.7281,45.6306,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. La Kiuva</name><description>Day 1 — Tuesday, July 28

A traditional Valle d&#x27;Aosta mountain restaurant en route from Milan to Chamonix. Welcome lunch stop for the group on arrival day.

Schedule:
Tuesday, July 28 12:30 PM: Welcome lunch at La Kiuva

Address: Arnad, Valle d&#x27;Aosta, Italy</description><Point><coordinates>7.7236,45.6197,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Hotel Lykke Chamonix Spa</name><description>Day 1 — Tuesday, July 28

The group hotel in Chamonix. Nordic-inspired spa hotel in the heart of the town, steps from the main street and cable car stations.

Schedule:
Tuesday, July 28 4:00 PM: Check in to Hotel Lykke Chamonix Spa
Tuesday, July 28 7:30 PM: Dinner at the hotel
Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1 12:30 PM: Lunch at hotel + change for concert
Thursday, July 30 8:00 AM: Check out — load bus

Address: 290 Rue Joseph Vallot, 74400 Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, France</description><Point><coordinates>6.8703,45.9238,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Centre des Congrès de Chamonix</name><description>Day 1 — Tuesday, July 28

Chamonix&#x27;s main convention and performance center. Used for rehearsals during the tour&#x27;s first days in the Alps.

Schedule:
Tuesday, July 28 5:30 PM: Rehearsal — Centre des Congrès

Address: 52 Rue Joseph Vallot, 74400 Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, France</description><Point><coordinates>6.8712,45.9242,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6. Aiguille du Midi</name><description>Day 2 — Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1

A 3,842-meter peak above Chamonix reached by the world&#x27;s highest vertical ascent cable car. Panoramic views of Mont Blanc and the entire Mont Blanc Massif — one of the most spectacular viewpoints in Europe.

Schedule:
Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1 9:00 AM: Visit Aiguille du Midi cable car

Address: Plan de l&#x27;Aiguille, 74400 Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, France</description><Point><coordinates>6.8877,45.8793,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Martigny Place Centrale</name><description>Day 2 — Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1

The central square of Martigny, Switzerland — a charming open-air concert setting in the Valais region. Concert #1 takes place here at 8pm on July 29.

Schedule:
Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1 3:00 PM: Transfer to Martigny, Switzerland — free time in groups
Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1 6:00 PM: Sound check and rehearsal — Place Centrale
Wednesday, July 29 ★ Concert #1 8:00 PM: Concert #1 — Place Centrale, Martigny

Address: Place Centrale, 1920 Martigny, Switzerland</description><Point><coordinates>7.0743,46.1017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8. Pont du Gard</name><description>Day 3 — Thursday, July 30

A UNESCO World Heritage Site and the best-preserved ancient Roman aqueduct in the world, built in the 1st century AD. Three tiers of arches span the Gardon River near Nîmes. An unmissable stop in Provence.

Schedule:
Thursday, July 30 12:00 PM: Stop at Pont du Gard — stretch, explore, photos
Thursday, July 30 1:15 PM: Lunch en route (service station)

Address: 400 Route du Pont du Gard, 30210 Vers-Pont-du-Gard, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.5353,43.9472,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9. Ibis Styles Arles Palais du Congrès</name><description>Day 3 — Thursday, July 30

The group hotel in Arles, located near the Palais des Congrès convention center.

Schedule:
Thursday, July 30 5:00 PM: Arrive Arles — check in to hotel
Thursday, July 30 7:00 PM: Dinner at the hotel
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 4:00 PM: Return to hotel — refresh for concert
Saturday, August 1 3:30 PM: Return to hotel — shower and change
Saturday, August 1 7:30 PM: Dinner at the hotel
Monday, August 3 9:00 AM: Check out — load bus

Address: 2 Rue de la Cavalerie, 13200 Arles, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.6243,43.6798,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10. Les Baux-de-Provence</name><description>Day 4 — Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2

One of the most dramatic villages in France, perched on a rocky outcrop with a ruined medieval citadel overlooking the Alpilles. Stunning panoramic views, ancient streets, and the famous Carrières de Lumières light show nearby.

Schedule:
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 10:00 AM: Guided tour of Les Baux-de-Provence
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 12:30 PM: Lunch in Les Baux (in groups)

Address: Les Baux-de-Provence, Bouches-du-Rhône, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.7957,43.7443,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>11. Restaurant La Madone</name><description>Day 4 — Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2

Restaurant for group dinner before Concert #2 on July 31 in the Provence region.

Schedule:
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 6:00 PM: Dinner at Restaurant La Madone

Address: Provence, France</description><Point><coordinates>5.54,43.72,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>12. Château de La Tour d&#x27;Aigues</name><description>Day 4 — Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2

A dramatic Renaissance château in the Luberon, partially ruined but majestically restored for cultural events. Concert #2 takes place here at 9pm on July 31 — an extraordinary outdoor setting.

Schedule:
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 7:30 PM: Sound check at Château de La Tour d&#x27;Aigues
Friday, July 31 ★ Concert #2 9:00 PM: Concert #2 — Château de La Tour d&#x27;Aigues

Address: Place du Château, 84240 La Tour-d&#x27;Aigues, France</description><Point><coordinates>5.5497,43.7243,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>13. Le Grau-du-Roi Beach</name><description>Day 5 — Saturday, August 1

A laid-back Mediterranean beach town at the mouth of the Rhône delta, about an hour from Arles. Wide sandy beaches, seafood restaurants, and a quintessential southern French coastal atmosphere.

Schedule:
Saturday, August 1 9:30 AM: Morning at the beach — Le Grau-du-Roi
Saturday, August 1 1:00 PM: Lunch in groups near the beach

Address: Le Grau-du-Roi, Gard, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.1356,43.5378,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>14. Arles</name><description>Day 5 — Saturday, August 1

A UNESCO-listed city in Provence famous for its remarkably well-preserved Roman monuments, Van Gogh&#x27;s most iconic paintings created here, and a vibrant arts scene. The Roman arena still hosts events today.

Schedule:
Saturday, August 1 5:00 PM: Free time in Arles — Roman Arena, Van Gogh sites, shopping

Address: Arles, Bouches-du-Rhône, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.6277,43.6767,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>15. Pont Saint-Bénézet (Pont d&#x27;Avignon)</name><description>Day 6 — Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3

The famous medieval bridge of Avignon, immortalized in the French folk song &#x27;Sur le pont d&#x27;Avignon.&#x27; Only four of the original 22 arches remain, jutting dramatically into the Rhône.

Schedule:
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 9:30 AM: Morning in Avignon — visit Pont Saint-Bénézet

Address: Rue Ferruce, 84000 Avignon, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.8047,43.9543,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>16. Palais des Papes</name><description>Day 6 — Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3

The largest Gothic palace in the world, built in the 14th century when Avignon was the seat of Western Christianity. A UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the most important medieval monuments in Europe.

Schedule:
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 10:45 AM: Visit Palais des Papes

Address: Place du Palais, 84000 Avignon, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.8085,43.9517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>17. Avignon</name><description>Day 6 — Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3

The &#x27;City of Popes&#x27; — a walled medieval city on the Rhône River with the magnificent Palais des Papes (Palace of the Popes), the famous Pont Saint-Bénézet bridge, and a UNESCO-listed historic center.

Schedule:
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 1:00 PM: Lunch — free time in Avignon
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 7:30 PM: Dinner in local restaurant

Address: Avignon, Vaucluse, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.8055,43.9493,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>18. Place de l&#x27;Horloge, Avignon</name><description>Day 6 — Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3

Avignon&#x27;s lively main square, fronted by the Town Hall and the opera house. One of two possible Concert #3 venues on August 2.

Schedule:
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 3:00 PM: Sound check — Place de l&#x27;Horloge, Avignon
Sunday, August 2 ★ Concert #3 5:00 PM: Concert #3 — Place de l&#x27;Horloge, Avignon (afternoon/early evening)

Address: Place de l&#x27;Horloge, 84000 Avignon, France</description><Point><coordinates>4.8063,43.9497,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>19. Marseille O Beach</name><description>Day 7 — Monday, August 3

A popular beach club on the Marseille waterfront — good stop for lunch between Arles and Nice.

Schedule:
Monday, August 3 11:00 AM: Lunch stop at Marseille O Beach

Address: 2 Promenade Georges Pompidou, 13008 Marseille, France</description><Point><coordinates>5.3819,43.2619,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>20. Saint-Paul-de-Vence</name><description>Day 7 — Monday, August 3

One of the most visited medieval villages in France — a perfectly preserved hilltop town with ramparts, art galleries, and stunning views over the Riviera. Home to the Fondation Maeght modern art museum.

Schedule:
Monday, August 3 1:30 PM: Afternoon in Saint-Paul-de-Vence or Nice (depending on concert location)

Address: Saint-Paul-de-Vence, Alpes-Maritimes, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.121,43.6973,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>21. NH Hotel Nice</name><description>Day 7 — Monday, August 3

The group hotel in Nice, centrally located for exploring the Riviera.

Schedule:
Monday, August 3 5:00 PM: Check in to NH Hotel Nice
Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4 3:00 PM: Return to hotel — change for concert
Wednesday, August 5 9:00 AM: Check out — load bus

Address: 3 Avenue des Phocéens, 06000 Nice, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.2676,43.6967,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>22. Nice</name><description>Day 7 — Monday, August 3

The capital of the French Riviera — a dazzling Mediterranean city of colorful architecture, a pebble beach promenade, an irresistible old town, and one of the great food markets in France.

Schedule:
Monday, August 3 7:00 PM: Dinner on own — in groups
Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4 7:00 PM: Dinner on own — in groups

Address: Nice, Alpes-Maritimes, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.262,43.7102,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>23. Vieux-Nice (Old Nice)</name><description>Day 8 — Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4

Nice&#x27;s old town — a labyrinth of narrow lanes, baroque churches, vivid ochre and pink facades, and the famous Cours Saleya flower and food market. A sensory feast. The guided tour ends at the market.

Schedule:
Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4 10:00 AM: Guided tour of Old Nice, ending at Cours Saleya Market

Address: Vieux-Nice, 06300 Nice, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.2769,43.6961,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>24. Cassa Nissa</name><description>Day 8 — Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4

A beloved restaurant in Old Nice serving traditional Niçois cuisine — pissaladière, salade niçoise, socca, and pasta with pistou. The group lunch spot on August 4.

Schedule:
Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4 12:30 PM: Lunch at Cassa Nissa — traditional Niçois cuisine

Address: 8 Rue Sainte-Réparate, 06300 Nice, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.2762,43.697,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>25. Nice Bandstand / Antibes / St-Raphaël</name><description>Day 8 — Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4

Concert #4 on August 4 — final venue TBD among Nice Bandstand, Antibes, or St-Raphaël. All are beautiful Riviera settings for an evening open-air performance.

Schedule:
Tuesday, August 4 ★ Concert #4 9:00 PM: Concert #4 — Nice (bandstand, Promenade area)

Address: Nice, Alpes-Maritimes, France</description><Point><coordinates>7.266,43.6953,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>26. Hotel Villa Borghi</name><description>Day 9 — Wednesday, August 5

A beautiful lakeside villa hotel in Northern Italy for the tour&#x27;s final night — pool, grounds, and a farewell dinner before the flight home.

Schedule:
Wednesday, August 5 1:00 PM: Arrive Hotel Villa Borghi — afternoon at pool and grounds
Wednesday, August 5 7:00 PM: Farewell Dinner
Thursday, August 6 7:00 AM: Depart for Milan Malpensa airport

Address: Via per Varese, 6, 21020 Azzate VA, Italy</description><Point><coordinates>8.7914,45.7746,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Tour route</name><Placemark><name>Bus/flight route</name><styleUrl>#route</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-73.7781,40.6413,0 8.7281,45.6306,0 7.7236,45.6197,0 6.8694,45.9237,0 7.0743,46.1017,0 6.8694,45.9237,0 4.5353,43.9472,0 4.6277,43.6767,0 4.7957,43.7443,0 5.5497,43.7243,0 4.6277,43.6767,0 4.1356,43.5378,0 4.6277,43.6767,0 4.8055,43.9493,0 4.6277,43.6767,0 5.3819,43.2619,0 7.121,43.6973,0 7.262,43.7102,0 8.7914,45.7746,0 8.7281,45.6306,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark></Folder></Document></kml>